# The app calls the API at the relative /api by default: in production Caddy
# routes /api and /socket.io to the backend on the same origin, and in
# development the Vite dev server proxies them (see vite.config.ts). Keep it
# that way: the refresh-token cookie and its CSRF double-submit only work when
# the app and the API share an origin.

# Dev only: where the Vite dev server proxies /api and /socket.io.
# VITE_DEV_PROXY_TARGET=http://localhost:5000

# Only for an unusual setup where the API lives on another origin
# (session restore after a reload will not work cross-origin).
# VITE_API_URL=https://api.example.com/api
